":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Discrete Applied Mathematics","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"42(2–3):177–201, 1993, define a hyperarc as “an ordered pair … of (possibly empty) disjoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subsets”; here either side may be empty and a vertex may be on both, the hypergraph form of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop (XGI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiHypergraph"},{"text":" allows both).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"DirectedHypergraph"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/GraphProtocols/Hypergraph/connectedComponents()":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/connectedComponents()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"connectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> [["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]]"}],"url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/graphprotocols\/hypergraph\/connectedcomponents()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The connected components: two vertices are together when a chain of hyperedges joins them."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Components are ordered by their least vertex index and list their vertices in index order;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an isolated vertex is alone, and an empty hyperedge joins nothing. No vertices, no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components."}],"title":"connectedComponents()"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/GraphProtocols/Hypergraph/degreeHistogram()":{"kind":"symbol","title":"degreeHistogram()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/Grap